Benchmark harness attribution
=============================

The benchmark scripts in this directory (`bench_latency.py`, `bench_memory.py`)
adapt the methodology and portions of the source of jcode's benchmark harnesses:

  - bench_startup_visible_ready.py
  - bench_memory_cli.py

by Jeremy Huang (https://github.com/1jehuang/jcode), used under the MIT License.

The techniques reused here — PTY-driven launches with terminal-capability
query replies, pyte-based screen modelling for first-visible/input-ready
detection, and total-PSS process-tree accounting via /proc/<pid>/smaps_rollup —
originate in that project. Synaps's harnesses are trimmed and made synaps-native
(daemon-aware session accounting via `synaps --attach`), but credit for the
approach and the original code belongs to jcode.

